## qf-sci2 | Quick-fire: science 2 | physics | 0 | - | qf-space
quiz 2 | What does a Geiger counter detect?
* Ionising radiation
o Magnetic fields
o Sound
o Air pressure
= Each particle triggers a click.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which colour of light has the most energy per photon?
* Violet
o Red
o Green
o Yellow
= Shorter wavelength, higher frequency, higher energy.
> Next

quiz 3 | What does E = mc² relate?
* Mass and energy
o Speed and time
o Force and acceleration
o Charge and current
= A small mass is equivalent to a huge energy.
> Next

quiz 3 | What is the unit of frequency?
* Hertz
o Joule
o Watt
o Tesla
= Cycles per second.
> Next

quiz 3 | Why do astronauts float in the ISS?
* They're in free fall along with the station
o There's no gravity in space
o The station is shielded from gravity
o Air pressure holds them up
= Everything falls together, so nothing presses on anything.
> Next

quiz 3 | What kind of mirror is used in car headlights?
* Concave (parabolic)
o Convex
o Flat
o Two-way
= A bulb at the focus produces a parallel beam.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which scientist proposed the three laws of planetary motion?
* Johannes Kepler
o Galileo
o Copernicus
o Tycho Brahe
= Based on Tycho Brahe's precise observations of Mars.
> Next

quiz 4 | What happens to the boiling point of water at high altitude?
* It decreases
o It increases
o It stays at 100°C
o Water can't boil
= Lower air pressure. On Everest's summit, water boils at about 70°C.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which wave property does NOT change when light enters glass?
* Frequency
o Speed
o Wavelength
o Direction (in general)
= Frequency is set by the source; speed and wavelength both drop.
> Next

quiz 4 | Who first measured the charge of the electron?
* Robert Millikan
o J. J. Thomson
o Ernest Rutherford
o Niels Bohr
= The oil drop experiment, 1909. Thomson measured charge-to-mass ratio.
