quiz 3 | Who led India's non-violent independence movement?
* Mahatma Gandhi
o Jawaharlal Nehru
o Muhammad Ali Jinnah
o Subhas Chandra Bose
= Independence came in 1947. Nehru became the first Prime Minister.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which war was fought between 1950 and 1953?
* The Korean War
o The Vietnam War
o The Suez Crisis
o The Falklands War
= It ended in an armistice, not a peace treaty.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which explorer's expedition first reached the South Pole?
* Roald Amundsen's
o Robert Falcon Scott's
o Ernest Shackleton's
o Edmund Hillary's
= December 1911, about five weeks before Scott's party.
> Next

quiz 4 | The Hundred Years' War actually lasted about…
* 116 years
o 100 years
o 99 years
o 140 years
= 1337 to 1453, with long truces.
> Next

quiz 4 | In which city was the Treaty of Versailles signed?
* Versailles, near Paris
o Vienna
o Berlin
o London
= 1919, ending WWI with Germany.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which ancient city was destroyed by Vesuvius in 79 AD?
* Pompeii (and Herculaneum)
o Rome
o Athens
o Carthage
= Pliny the Younger described the eruption in letters.
